---
// Generated by packages/calibration-lab/lab/figures.py from results.json. Do not edit by hand.
interface Props { caption?: boolean }
const { caption = true } = Astro.props;
---

<figure>
  <svg class="fig" viewBox="0 0 660 380" role="img" aria-label="Each model plotted by resolution against reliability.">
    <line x1="66.0" y1="30" x2="66.0" y2="332" class="grid" />
    <text x="66.0" y="352" class="tick mid">0.00</text>
    <line x1="250.67" y1="30" x2="250.67" y2="332" class="grid" />
    <text x="250.67" y="352" class="tick mid">0.05</text>
    <line x1="435.33" y1="30" x2="435.33" y2="332" class="grid" />
    <text x="435.33" y="352" class="tick mid">0.10</text>
    <line x1="620.0" y1="30" x2="620.0" y2="332" class="grid" />
    <text x="620.0" y="352" class="tick mid">0.15</text>
    <line x1="66" y1="332.0" x2="620" y2="332.0" class="grid" />
    <text x="56" y="336.0" class="tick end">0.0001</text>
    <line x1="66" y1="231.33" x2="620" y2="231.33" class="grid" />
    <text x="56" y="235.33" class="tick end">0.001</text>
    <line x1="66" y1="130.67" x2="620" y2="130.67" class="grid" />
    <text x="56" y="134.67" class="tick end">0.01</text>
    <line x1="66" y1="30.0" x2="620" y2="30.0" class="grid" />
    <text x="56" y="34.0" class="tick end">0.1</text>
    <line x1="66" y1="332" x2="620" y2="332" class="axis" />
    <line x1="66" y1="30" x2="66" y2="332" class="axis" />
    <text x="343.0" y="372" class="label mid">resolution: how much it knows →</text>
    <text x="14" y="181.0" class="label mid" transform="rotate(-90 14 181.0)">reliability: how dishonest (log) →</text>
    <circle cx="94.09" cy="281.01" r="4.5" fill="var(--viz-amber)" stroke="var(--bg)" stroke-width="2"><title>keyword rates: reliability 0.0003, resolution 0.0076, AUC 0.608</title></circle>
    <text x="102.09" y="285.01" class="note">keyword rates</text>
    <circle cx="385.94" cy="71.92" r="4.5" fill="var(--viz-rose)" stroke="var(--bg)" stroke-width="2"><title>naive Bayes: reliability 0.0383, resolution 0.0866, AUC 0.850</title></circle>
    <text x="393.94" y="75.92" class="note">naive Bayes</text>
    <circle cx="456.13" cy="261.64" r="4.5" fill="var(--viz-amber)" stroke="var(--bg)" stroke-width="2"><title>TF-IDF + LR: reliability 0.0005, resolution 0.1056, AUC 0.872</title></circle>
    <circle cx="434.13" cy="223.58" r="4.5" fill="var(--viz-amber)" stroke="var(--bg)" stroke-width="2"><title>TF-IDF + GBM: reliability 0.0012, resolution 0.0997, AUC 0.863</title></circle>
    <circle cx="460.21" cy="256.92" r="4.5" fill="var(--viz-amber)" stroke="var(--bg)" stroke-width="2"><title>probe: reliability 0.0006, resolution 0.1067, AUC 0.874</title></circle>
    <text x="452.21" y="272.92" class="note" text-anchor="end">probe</text>
    <circle cx="455.3" cy="186.46" r="4.5" fill="var(--viz-amber)" stroke="var(--bg)" stroke-width="2"><title>probe, no L2: reliability 0.0028, resolution 0.1054, AUC 0.871</title></circle>
    <text x="463.3" y="190.46" class="note">probe, no L2</text>
    <circle cx="460.69" cy="198.05" r="4.5" fill="var(--viz-amber)" stroke="var(--bg)" stroke-width="2"><title>MLP head: reliability 0.0021, resolution 0.1069, AUC 0.870</title></circle>
    <circle cx="465.53" cy="177.38" r="4.5" fill="var(--viz-amber)" stroke="var(--bg)" stroke-width="2"><title>Jev (mock): reliability 0.0034, resolution 0.1082, AUC 0.873</title></circle>
    <text x="473.53" y="171.38" class="note">Jev (mock)</text>
    <circle cx="501.39" cy="262.79" r="4.5" fill="var(--viz-blue)" stroke="var(--bg)" stroke-width="2"><title>oracle: reliability 0.0005, resolution 0.1179, AUC 0.891</title></circle>
    <text x="509.39" y="266.79" class="note">oracle</text>
  </svg>
  {caption && <figcaption>Murphy&#x27;s split of the Brier score puts every model on two independent axes (hover a dot for its name). Keyword rates are honest and nearly useless; naive Bayes knows a lot and lies about it (reliability 0.038). Down and to the right is better.</figcaption>}
</figure>

<style>
  .fig { width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; margin: 1.6rem auto 0.6rem; }
  .fig text { font-family: var(--font-jetbrains); fill: var(--text-dim); }
  .fig .tick { font-size: 12px; }
  .fig .label { font-size: 12.5px; fill: var(--text-muted); }
  .fig .mid { text-anchor: middle; }
  .fig .end { text-anchor: end; }
  .fig .grid { stroke: var(--border); stroke-width: 1; }
  .fig .axis { stroke: var(--border); stroke-width: 1.5; }
  .fig .ref { stroke: var(--text-muted); stroke-width: 1.5; stroke-dasharray: 4 4; fill: none; }
  .fig .series { fill: none; stroke-width: 2; stroke-linecap: round; stroke-linejoin: round; }
  .fig .key { font-size: 12.5px; fill: var(--text); }
  .fig .note { font-size: 11.5px; fill: var(--text-muted); }
  .fig .big { font-size: 13px; fill: var(--text); }
  figcaption {
    font-family: var(--font-jetbrains);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    max-width: 36rem;
    margin: 0 auto 2.2rem;
    text-align: center;
  }
</style>
